  "security_implications": "The key registers (indices 11-31) are made write-only to software (.re tied to 0, .qs left unconnected), but no hardware write protection gating is present. If the external logic allows a key write during HMAC operation, the key could be corrupted or replaced, leading to forged MACs. The digest registers have a connected software read path (.qs), and if read during an active digest update, the intermediate hash state may be exposed, facilitating collision or preimage attacks. Missing assignment of addr_hint could indicate incomplete decode coverage, potentially leaving registers accessible via unintended addressing.",
